+# Intent: index complete managed Arrow inserts once
+
+Date: 2026-11-13. Source: `ba855f7995b2685182ed1331bcf6703d73089c4a`.
+Requestor: repository user (performance improvements with subagents).
+Status: experiment under implementation, pending correctness and performance evidence.
+
+The current managed Arrow writer stages complete first-insert row images, then
+notifies every row a second time while constructing the final private index.
+The [baseline](validation.md) attributes about 0.69 seconds of a 1.71-second
+single-call diagnostic to that second pass. Eliminate it only when one empty
+private index can observe every complete immutable image's first insertion.
+
+Preserve public-call atomicity, leased admission before input consumption,
+metadata/source fences, bounded batches and exact final readiness proofs.
+Exclude SQL writes, imports/provenance, Flex and retained operations. Do not
+coalesce calls, change storage format or weaken source-index validation.
+
+See [specification](spec.md) and [plan](plan.md). No release or human review
+approval is claimed by this record.
