+## Candidate correctness, first bounded block
+
+The narrow candidate compiled and passed 47 selected tests/subtests with zero
+skips/failures on the same owned Software TLS/RESP3 fixture with effective
+4x QPF reverified immediately before execution. Coverage includes first-insert
+index timing and complete 513×105 images, a lost acknowledged row reply without
+replay, zero-row deferral, unknown CREATE abort and reclamation, private overwrite
+rebuild, reader failure/cancellation, late TAG truncation/NaN metadata, typed
+query-ACL fallback versus transport/warning refusal, existing SQL notification
+bounds/readiness and SQL cold/hot/SCRIPT FLUSH notification-cache behavior.
+
+The first attempt had one leaf test-observer failure: typed ACL ingestion
+succeeded but the newly added initial-scan counter was attached only to the
+maintenance pool, while Search used the execution pool. The observer was fixed
+to instrument both existing transports. Production source was unchanged between
+that attempt and the 47-pass rerun. Both raw attempts are retained privately.
+
+A separate related lifecycle selection passed 35 tests/subtests, with six skips
+and no failures. It covered ingest admission, import atomic batches/index policy,
+provenance joins and Arrow-replace import identity. Two skipped journal-ACL
+preflight cases require dedicated restricted principals; four retained-operation
+cases require an explicit verified Cluster URI. Those skipped capabilities are
+not claimed as tested. Additional retained-Arrow/race/ACL checks and matched
+candidate native measurements remain pending; this is not acceptance evidence
+for a performance gain.
+
+## Candidate actual ACL, retained Arrow and race block
+
+The subsequent combined `go test -race -count=1 -p 1` selection passed
+**59 tests/subtests, zero skips/failures**, in 27.4 seconds (54.5 seconds including
+private principal setup and cleanup). Go 1.27.3 darwin/arm64; same owned Software
+fixture and effective 4x QPF, noeviction, strict data-plane TLS/RESP3.
+
+Four temporary Software principals independently denied EVALSHA, FT.SEARCH,
+HDEL and ZREM. Each principal's PING/EVAL positive control and intended command
+denial were verified before tests. Actual EVAL-only Arrow/SQL notification
+fallback, write-only Arrow publication, import-journal permission preflight and
+cleanup passed. Write-only Arrow built its early index and selected exactly
+one typed query-ACL initial-scan replacement, with no notification pass;
+independent admin full-fetch/type/value validation preserved all 513×105 values.
+
+A non-Cluster retained-Arrow regression verified that prepare creates no index,
+resume consumes no further input, and the deferred final CREATE plus three
+notification batches preserves all 513×105 values. This covers the functional
+retained-operation exclusion without claiming the earlier skipped Cluster-only
+API/topology scenarios. The combined race selection also re-exercised input
+admission, unknown replies, cancellation, index-policy/provenance and source
+refresh identity. The four temporary users, role mappings, ACLs and roles were
+removed; effective 4x QPF was reverified after cleanup. Only the owned disposable
+DB was reset; emptiness was asserted and all clients closed before ending the
+exclusive correctness slot.
+
+Candidate performance acceptance remains pending matched native measurements.
